WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This Friday, June 19th,
is Juneteenth,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.236 line:92%
a holiday that celebrates

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
the end of slavery
in the United States.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
But not everyone
is familiar with it.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, here is "Late Night" write
Amber Ruffin

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.514
with answers to frequently asked
Juneteenth questions.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's been a lot of tal
about Juneteenth

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:17.751 size:81% position:41% line:92%
the last couple weeks.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
But some people have
never heard of it before,

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they have questions
about it

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they feel
embarrassed to ask.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.727
So, I let some folks mail me
their questions anonymously,

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:31.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm gonna answer them
right now.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.032 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.366 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Question number one.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.101 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"What is Juneteenth?"

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:38.772 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Okay. Great question.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
Juneteenth is the anniversar
of June 19th, 1865.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the day the last
American slaves were freed -

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:47.580
otherwise known as "the last
good day in Black history.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I'm just kidding
a little bit.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the day we celebrate
our freedom,

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
and see how far
we've come.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.188 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Okay. Next question.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Didn't the
Emancipation Proclamation

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
free the slaves
in 1863?

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why, then, is Juneteenth based
on a day on 1865?"

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.131 line:92%
Glad you caught that. Yes.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.401
After slaves had been freed,
and the Civil War was over

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
some people in Texas
still had slaves,

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
and would not
let them go.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
They held on to them
for an extra 2 1/2 years.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
they were arrested

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
for brazenly
disobeying the law.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just kidding.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
Slave owners have never
been punished.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.616 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Okay. Next question.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How do you
celebrate Juneteenth?"

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Great.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, now, usually,
Juneteenth is celebrated

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:33.293
during, like, a block party,
with fun music and good food

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
where a little girl sings
"Life Ev'ry Voice And Sing,"

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.597 size:75% position:38% line:92%
while I shout at her

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You had better get
that song sung, baby."

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this year,
because of COVID,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.138
we're all gonna celebrate
by watching Alicia Keys

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
and John Legend battle it ou
on "Versus."

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's just a real
answer for you.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
Google it.
Okay.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If I'm White,
can I celebrate Juneteenth?"

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:55.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
White people can
celebrate Juneteenth.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.285 size:78% position:39%
But you got to do it
by going like this --

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, no. My slaves.
My precious slaves."

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.523 size:78% position:39% line:92%
No, I'm just kidding.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
You celebrate it
by being thankful

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
that your Black
friends and family

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
are free to be
whatever they want to be.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, you do your best
to make that statement true.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.237 size:75% position:38% line:92%
No costumes, please.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:17.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If Juneteenth falls
on a weekend,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
do we get
that Monday off, too?"

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, now, I don't have
the authority

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:30.350
to make that decision, but I'm
gonna say, "Yes. Definitely.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.085 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Okay. Next question.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Does the holiday Juneteenth
make up for all the --"

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.157 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No. No.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're not gonna
finish that question.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The answer is "no,"

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter what
the end of it was.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.663 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.666 size:81% position:41%
"Why am I only hearing
about Juneteenth now?"

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay.
Ask your Black friends.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just kidding.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:51.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can tell by your questio
you don't have any.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.505 line:92%
But you should make some.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're fun, and you might
get invited to a block party

00:02:54.908 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just make sure not to celebrat
it by wearing a costume.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:01.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:03.016 size:78% position:39%
"Is this gonna become
one of those holidays

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.785 size:78% position:39%
that's just an excuse
to hold car sales?"

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:08.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
No. Please don't
cheapen it like that.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although, I do need
a new car,

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:13.226
'cause if think I'm getting back
on the subway anytime soon

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have lost
your dang mind.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, maybe.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.733 size:88% position:44%
"So, now that Juneteenth
is an official holiday,

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
what else can we do
to address systemic racism?"

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay. Hire Black people.
Defund the police.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.842
Call out White supremacy.
Fight the power. Be anti-racist.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And most importantly,
stop asking Black people

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
how you can address
systemic racism.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have time
to answer all your questions

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:39.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to go
buy a car.

